], "model": {"prior_margin": 15.19, "prior_sd": 5.11, "poll_margin": null, "poll_sd": null, "poll_weight": 0.0, "fundamentals": {"margin": 15.14, "lean": 4.0, "environment": 8.2, "incumbency": 2.0, "money": 0.94}, "rating_margin": 15.22, "sigma_race": 6.7, "sigma_total": 7.45, "baseline_margin": 15.19, "analyst_adjustment": 0.01, "key_factors": ["All nine expert ratings call the seat Safe or Solid Democratic", "Prediction markets price Scholten's win probability in the low-to-mid 90s", "Scholten holds a steep fundraising edge: $1.36M cash on hand versus DeBoer's $361K", "No public general-election polls; district fundamentals lean Democratic in a favorable environment"], "rationale": "Scholten combines incumbency, a large cash advantage, and a district that now leans Democratic in an environment favorable to her party, while raters unanimously rate the seat Safe or Solid Democratic and markets price her chances in the low-to-mid 90s. DeBoer's outsider primary win and its immediate Republican consolidation have not visibly moved the race's fundamentals.", "watch": "DeBoer's moderate positioning, including public breaks with Trump on some issues, could resonate with Kent County ticket-splitters and tighten the race if the national environment shifts late.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Hillary Scholten (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Democratic incumbent Hillary Scholten seeks re-election in this Grand Rapids-area West Michigan seat, facing Republican Terri DeBoer, an outsider who won her primary promising to flip the longtime Republican district back, plus Green candidate Joe Jock. The district carries a modest Democratic lean, and the 2026 political environment favors Scholten's party.\n\nNo public polls test the matchup, but other evidence points clearly her way. Every major ratings outlet calls the race Safe or Solid Democratic, and prediction markets give her 